mportant information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le01ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Making and Responding to Simple Requests", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You often make simple requests by asking a question with the modals <span class=\"italic\">can</span> or <span class=\"italic\">could</span> followed by a verb.<br/><br/>You can respond to requests with expressions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Making Requests\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Responding to Requests\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can you describe the food for me?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Absolutely!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Could you make me some tacos?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Sure, I'd love to!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can you help me for a second?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">No problem!</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you talk about things, actions or events in the past, you use the Simple Past tense.<br/><br/>To form the Simple Past tense, you add <span class=\"strong\">-d</span> or <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> to regular verbs like <span class=\"italic\">worked</span>, or change the verb for irregular verbs like <span class=\"italic\">went </span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span = class\"italic\">We worked hard, but we had some free time to explore.</span>", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span = class\"italic\">I loved Mexico. </span>", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span = class\"italic\">We went all the way down to Baja, California.</span>", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "taco", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a flat, round food made of corn, typically Mexican, filled with a mixture of meat and vegetables", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Mexican food is spicy, often served with tacos.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le01ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear to talk about food and holidays.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "shrimp", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a type of seafood", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can put almost anything into a taco, like meat, shrimp or cooked vegetables. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le01ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pork", "type": "name"}, {"content": "meat that comes from a pig", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My favorite taco is with pork and pineapple.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le01ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pineapple", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large tropical fruit with a thick skin", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Tacos with pork and pineapple are called Pastor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le01ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "free time", "type": "name"}, {"content": "time without responsibilities", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We had some free time to explore.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le01ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to describe", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to explain in detail", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Can you describe the food for me?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le01ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "You are catching up with a friend. Start your e-mail with \u201cDear ... \u201d", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write what you did yesterday or the day before yesterday.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write what you did last week.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write what you did last month.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe how you felt.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Conclude your e-mail with a line like \u201cSee you soon!\u201d", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your e-mail to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about what I did in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe my feelings.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my e-mail aloud.", "type": "text"}]}]}